			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mstdn.social/@mattwilcox\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mattwilcox</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Yes, it's hilarious but it's also quite a good summary of how many people actually seem to think about open source and the maintainers behind the projects. They still see themselves as customers with the same demands as if they had paid for the product.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
