			},
			"date": "2026-03-12T16:20:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> The thinking about ‘free’ stuff is really backwards. I’ve had people contact me about potential commissions who think that because they plan to release the font under OFL that means I will charge less or donate my time to their project.</p><p>I have been kicking around an idea for a blog post about the economics of creating a typeface and then surrendering most rights to enable other people to use it at no cost. Provisionally entitled ‘It’s free, so it costs more.’</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
